      "metric_semantics": "Headline abstention metrics use the raw registered actions unchanged, exactly as in the PER-32 published statistics: correct_abstention_rate is exact equality of actual_action and expected_action over Gold rows whose expected_action is not 'answer'; erroneous_abstention_rate counts actual_action != 'answer' over Gold rows whose expected_action is 'answer', so a null actual_action counts as erroneous there and can never be credited as a correct abstention. The PER-32 auditor's reject_action->abstain / null->answer folding was applied only inside the implementation-equivalence fixture fed to the frozen v1 scorer, never to the published headline numbers, and is therefore not part of this contract."
